      statement: "76% of nodes (25584 of 33830) have supply_chain.reason='test path matches (?:^|/)tests?/' — i.e. they are classified as test-tier symbols. Only 6180 nodes (18.3%) are from first-party src/. The behavior map is dominated by test code. Comparable: 1144 unresolved external (3.4%), 480 internal_dep (1.4%), 358 default-no-pattern (1.1%), 82 dependency declarations (0.2%), 2 npm_package (negligible)"  # 0455
      root_cause: "Tests are not de-emphasized in the behavior map by default. Consumers wanting production-code-only views must filter is_test_file=True themselves (e.g., test-coverage subcommand does this internally, dead-code-maybe optionally via --seeds). The ratio reflects that hypergumbo's own test corpus is large (~5x production code), but downstream consumers and sketches may want a default that excludes or compresses test nodes"  # 0455
